    "body": "Review of PR #3890 found code facts for this issue. With a Linear lead, the lead start is on the ring line beside the finished wall (`arc_leads.rs:26-28`, seam mid-run). Under G40, the wall-side Plunge `graze` at `e2`, the wall-side `wall_arc`, the bore-side `dive_link` to `e2` and the bore-side Arc all run there at the nominal radius. A register larger than the nominal radius, or a positive wear value, cuts the wall by the difference. With a Perpendicular lead, the start is at least one radius out on the air normal. Details: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/pull/3890 (review notes 1 and 2).",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
